# People and Employment native module candidate

Exact base: `0f812243c4af461bfd3685f8413ded84456f282b`. Author `/root/integration_security`; root independently reviews/adopts tests and admits implementation. This is a concrete module candidate, not another release roadmap. No product change, build, test execution or runtime acceptance is claimed in this packet.

The existing `render_screens(ShippingScreens, UiScreen::Hr)` shows disconnected Person/Employment API links and suppresses an Employment read failure whenever any Person row is present. Improve this existing production renderer first. Native `<details>/<summary>` opens each Person inspector in the directory; related Employment records use their real `person_id`, distinct object identities and stable fragment anchors. Normal API source links remain available as secondary links, preserving existing accepted head/navigation tests. No new destination or submit is exposed before its real transport is mounted.

## Production presentation

Use the shared light theme, Korean-readable type, restrained border/shadow, 8/12/16/24 spacing, blue focused controls, tabular revision/date values, readable wrapping and minimum 44px disclosure targets. Classes are scoped `people-*`, `person-*`, `employment-*`, `workflow-*`; root owns their shared stylesheet integration. Directory header is `사람과 고용`, subtitle explains these are the records currently available in this scope. Counts are only the length of each authorized projection, labelled `표시 중`; never total employees, active workers or permission counts inferred from absent fields.

Directory and Employment sections retain independent Omitted/Empty/Failure/Rows semantics. A failed section displays its own error and ordinary `/hr` retry while the healthy section remains usable. Denied sections, counts and controls are absent. A section failure never becomes an empty result or hides behind healthy rows.

Each Person disclosure has an initial glyph derived from its authorized name (not a fake avatar), name, secondary legal name only if different, visible revision and record identity in the expanded inspector. Read-only details show `표시 이름`, `법적 이름`, `기록 버전`; missing names are explicitly unavailable, never reconstructed from Employment or Account. Related Employment entries show the actual effective opening date and version, with the exact original instant retained in data attributes; headings say `고용 기록`, not inferred ACTIVE status. Employment's available Person relation links only if that Person is in the same authorized projection. Unbound/undisclosed relation is honest text, not an invented Person, guessed name or broken route. Namesakes have separate UUID identities. Each Person inspector is the native details element with id person-UUID; each Employment inspector is details with id employment-UUID. Relationship links are checked inside each owning inspector, including absence from a namesake, not just anywhere in the page.

On wide screens the section layout uses balanced two-column cards and an expanded inspector remains adjacent to directory context; on narrow screens the DOM reading order is directory then Employment, without horizontal scrolling. Native disclosures provide keyboard activation and exposed expanded state. Focus-visible outlines, clear headings and labelled definition lists preserve screen-reader semantics. No static list hydration, table-only content hidden on mobile, icon-only actions, sample business numbers or messenger overlay.

## Exact implementation partition

Agent after this directory admission owns new `backend/crates/payroll/ui/src/people.rs` and reviewed `people_tests.rs`. Typed forms have the complete design below but receive their own accepted target and real mount before any implementation; no unmounted form scaffolding is created. `people.rs` owns directory and inspector components; it consumes existing `PersonView`, `EmploymentView`, `ScreenSection` and does not expand their closed projection. Root alone changes `lib.rs`: module registration, delegates `hr_body` to the new renderer, and shared CSS. Existing DirectoryPeople/Employments can be removed by root only after all retained assertions pass. Root also owns any App route, generated BUCK/resource registration and lockfile.

No Company `native_account.*`, generated contracts, SQL, migrations, app owner or shared style edits by this agent. A pure module helper returns `AnyView`; root retains whole HTML/document/CSP and workspace shell. No new framework, compiler, demo binary or parallel rendering stack.

## Complete typed create/change form design for the next real mounted target

The separately rendered form components use real contract fields, and are mounted only with a real server-produced action binding. A read-authorized directory must not imply create/change authority. Form composition is native Leptos; standard labels/inputs/selects/fieldsets, plain-language consequences, evidence beside the confirmation, and preserved input after rejection. Root supplies authorized reference choices and a mounted native form command bridge as the following wiring step; module code cannot synthesize endpoint success or expose unbound submission.

- Person create/revise: actual targets `people.create_person` and `people.revise_person`. Inputs are explicit name fields inside `attributes`; revise retains actual `person_id` and `expected_revision`. Optional `employee_id` comes only from a separately authorized, uniquely resolved Employee reference. `PersonView.id` never stands in for Employee ID. Empty Employee selection means deliberately unbound Person. No phone, national ID, bank or salary fields from the closed read projection.
- Appointment: `hr.appoint` uses actual `employee_id`, `valid_from` and `attributes{company,org_unit_id,job_position_id,employment_status}`. Existing Employment changes use `hr.promote` or `hr.transfer` with `employment_id`, never invented `create_employment`, `hr.exit` or a made-up POST to the read collection. Company is the owner-provided contract value; OrgUnit/JobPosition are actual authorized references, with names supplied by their owners. No free-text UUID entry or label-as-identity conversion.
- Effective time is explicit `datetime-local` plus a server-supplied labelled time zone/offset and validated RFC3339 conversion at the bridge; never assume browser local zone or silently turn a Korean date into UTC midnight. Dates belong to these separate form pages, not a speculative temporal picker on the current directory (existing tests forbid that).
- Reuse exact existing canonical `ActionRequest`: registered object_type_id, instance_id where appropriate, stable command_id, current expected_revision on change, reason and params. The binding supplies the real registered action key and preflight/execute route. Evidence uses actual preflight gates; checklist acknowledgment is an explicit user control if required, and four-eyes reference is owner-selected. No hardcoded approval true or invented object_type UUID.
- Form outcome type distinguishes Editing, Pending, Committed(receipt and actual refs), Rejected(field/global errors), Conflict(current authorized comparison), and Unknown(original command recovery). UI never creates a receipt or assigns committed state locally. Confirmation must show exact immutable intent before execution; edits after dispatch require the owning recovery protocol, not a newly generated command on timeout.

Actual routes are `/api/v1/ontology/actions/{action_key}/preflight` and `/api/v1/ontology/actions/{action_key}/execute` as confirmed at `ontology/rest/src/lib.rs:537–538`; module must receive rather than invent this transport binding. Native Account-to-business authorization remains a separate real bridge obligation; no forged legacy principal or implicit Employee/Account conversion is permitted. Do not implement unmounted form components or placeholders. Freeze the exact native command bridge and mounted form routes with independent reviewed tests first; then implement the form and bridge together in its admitted target. No dead create/change button is added to the shipping page.

## Executable RED candidate

`tests.patch` adds only `#[cfg(test)] mod people_tests;` to existing `lib.rs` and one new test source. It calls the existing public renderer and existing DTOs; no phantom symbol, database fixture or missing infrastructure is used as RED. Root's review/admission command:

`tools/buck2 run //backend/crates/payroll/ui:console-payroll-ui-unit -- --exact people_tests::people_directory_preserves_independent_failure_next_to_authorized_rows`

First discover exactly that leaf with the same executable using `--list --exact`; record one discovered and executed test. Expected semantic RED: Person name renders, but `고용 기록을 불러오지 못했습니다` and section retry do not. Both sibling-failure directions and both denied-sibling directions are covered; retry must be inside the failed labelled subsection, not satisfied by the global navigation. Public Rows(empty) normalizes exactly to authorized Empty. The complete six-leaf module additionally checks keyboard inspector identity/actual relationships, denied section omission, separate authorized empty states, escaping, exact instant/revision preservation, no unneeded WASM or fake links. Existing 13+ source unit leaves and real route/browser checks remain unchanged.

Form-specific tests will be submitted against the admitted actual form types before exposing their routes: exact named fields/action mapping and original IDs, omitted unauthorized controls, no employee/person identity coercion, stale/unknown original-command retention, preflight refusal preservation, Korean/long-name escaping and original effective instant. Do not fabricate an executable current-boundary RED for missing form APIs; root freezes the bridge fixture/oracle first.

